prompt:
Audit the following smart contract code and identify any Unchecked Return Value / Silent ERC20 Failure vulnerabilities:

function payout(address token, address to, uint256 amount) external {
    IERC20(token).transfer(to, amount);
}

completion:
### Vulnerability Analysis
- Category: Unchecked Return Value / Silent ERC20 Failure (CWE-252)
- Severity: MEDIUM
- Explanation: Calling standard transfer/transferFrom without verifying boolean return or using SafeERC20.

### Patched Implementation:
```solidity
using SafeERC20 for IERC20;
function payout(address token, address to, uint256 amount) external {
    IERC20(token).safeTransfer(to, amount);
}
```

